  "output": "## Performance Analysis — Platizio (Next.js 16 / React 19 marketing site)\n\nFirst, an important scoping note: this is a fully static marketing site — no database, no API routes, no `fetch` calls at request time. Every route uses `generateStaticParams` + `dynamicParams = false` (`src/app/products/[slug]/page.tsx`, `src/app/insights/[slug]/page.tsx`), so there's no N+1 query pattern to find because there are no queries. I focused the review on what's actually present: client-side re-renders, memory-leak-shaped bugs, duplicated components, and redundant work.\n\n### 1. N+1 query patterns — Not applicable\nNo database/ORM/fetch layer exists. Content lives in TS modules (`src/lib/articles.ts`, `src/lib/products.tsx`) and is baked into static HTML at build time via `generateStaticParams`. This is already the correct pattern — nothing to fix here.\n\n### 2. Unnecessary React re-renders\n\n**`src/components/sections/Products.tsx:149-197` and `src/components/pages/ProductsIndex.tsx:103-143`** — hover state lives in the parent (`activeIndex`/`previewIndex`), and `ProductRow` isn't memoized. Hovering any one of the 5 rows re-renders the parent, which re-creates all 5 `<ProductRow>` elements (new inline `onActivate`/`onDeactivate` closures every time), forcing React to re-render every row instead of just the one whose `active` prop actually changed:\n\n```tsx\n// Products.tsx / ProductsIndex.tsx — today\n{PRODUCTS.map((product, i) => (\n  <ProductRow\n    active={activeIndex === i}\n    onActivate={() => activate(i)}       // new function identity every render\n    onDeactivate={() => setActiveIndex(null)}\n  />\n))}\n```\n\nFix — memoize the row and pass stable callbacks (index-curried via `useCallback`, or better, let each row own its own hover state locally with CSS `group-hover` and only lift the *preview* index up via a light `onMouseEnter` that doesn't need to be recreated per-render):\n\n```tsx\nconst ProductRow = memo(function ProductRow({ product, index, active, onActivate, onDeactivate }: Props) {\n  /* ... */\n});\n\nconst activate = useCallback((i: number) => {\n  setActiveIndex(i);\n  setPreviewIndex(i);\n}, []);\nconst deactivate = useCallback(() => setActiveIndex(null), []);\n```\n\nWith only 5 items the runtime cost today is trivial, but it's the textbook \"lift state up, forget to memo down\" pattern and is worth fixing since the same bug is duplicated in two files (see §5).\n\n### 3. Caching opportunities\n\nThe existing caching story is actually good and worth preserving, not undoing:\n- Full SSG via `generateStaticParams`/`dynamicParams = false` for products & articles.\n- `next/image` with `fill` + `sizes` for all photos (`AboutPage.tsx`).\n- `MarketConstellation` (the heaviest dependency — three.js + r3f) is lazy-loaded client-only via `dynamic(() => import(...), { ssr: false })` in `Hero.tsx:16-19`, keeping it out of the SSR bundle and off pages that don't need it.\n\nOne real gap: **`src/components/pages/AboutPage.tsx:406-414`** doesn't reuse `SiteShell`. Every other interior page (`ProductsIndex`, `InsightsIndex`, `ContactPage`, `ProductPage`, `ArticlePage`) goes through `SiteShell`, which deliberately *skips* `IntroProvider`/`Preloader` — the comment in `SiteShell.tsx:9-12` says so explicitly (\"interior pages skip the drenched preloader so navigation stays instant\"). `AboutPage` instead hand-rolls `IntroProvider > SmoothScroll > Nav/Footer`, which re-triggers the full ~1.8s preloader curtain (RAF loop + `overflow: hidden` on `<html>`) on every visit to `/about` — contrary to the site's own stated design and wasted client work on a page that doesn't need it:\n\n```tsx\n// AboutPage.tsx — bypasses SiteShell, re-instantiates the preloader\nexport default function AboutPage() {\n  return (\n    <IntroProvider>\n      <SmoothScroll>\n        <AboutContent />\n      </SmoothScroll>\n    </IntroProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nFix: render `<SiteShell><AboutHero/>...</SiteShell>` like the other interior pages, unless the preloader-on-About is an intentional product decision — worth confirming with whoever owns the design.\n\n### 4. Memory leaks\n\n**`src/components/Preloader.tsx:37-61`** — real bug. The `raf` handle is reused for both the animation loop *and* is the only thing cancelled on unmount, but the `window.setTimeout` scheduled once loading completes is never captured or cleared:\n\n```tsx\nconst tick = (now: number) => {\n  // ...\n  if (t < 1) {\n    raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n  } else {\n    window.setTimeout(() => {          // ← id never stored\n      if (!doneRef.current) { doneRef.current = true; onDone(); }\n      setVisible(false);\n      document.documentElement.style.overflow = \"\";\n    }, HOLD_MS);\n  }\n};\n\nraf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\nreturn () => {\n  cancelAnimationFrame(raf);           // only cancels the RAF, not the pending timeout\n  document.documentElement.style.overflow = \"\";\n};\n```\n\nIf the component unmounts during that 280ms `HOLD_MS` window (fast client-side nav away, React Fast Refresh in dev, etc.), the timeout still fires later and calls `onDone()`/`setVisible` against a torn-down closure — a dangling timer that outlives its component. Fix:\n\n```tsx\nlet raf = 0;\nlet holdTimer = 0;\nconst tick = (now: number) => {\n  // ...\n  if (t < 1) {\n    raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n  } else {\n    holdTimer = window.setTimeout(() => { /* ... */ }, HOLD_MS);\n  }\n};\nraf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\nreturn () => {\n  cancelAnimationFrame(raf);\n  window.clearTimeout(holdTimer);\n  document.documentElement.style.overflow = \"\";\n};\n```\n\nEverything else checked (`SmoothScroll`'s Lenis+RAF loop, `MarketConstellation`'s `geometry.dispose()`, pointer/matchMedia listeners in `MarketConstellation`/`Nav`) has correct cleanup — no leaks there.\n\n### 5. Redundant computations / duplicated code\n\nTwo components are near-byte-identical duplicates, meaning the client bundle ships (and the team maintains) the same logic twice:\n\n- **`ProductRow`**: `src/components/sections/Products.tsx:53-147` vs `src/components/pages/ProductsIndex.tsx:12-101` — same markup, same hover-sweep animation, same active/preview state pattern.\n- **The rotating-compass CTA**: `src/components/sections/CTA.tsx` vs `src/components/site/ContactCTA.tsx` — identical `TICKS` computation (`Array.from({ length: 36 }, ...)` with the same trig) and identical SVG/markup, just with `ContactCTA` made prop-configurable.\n\nExtracting each pair into one shared component (`ContactCTA` already looks like the intended generalization of `CTA`, and `ProductsIndex`'s row could just reuse `Products`' row with a `PRODUCT_MAP`-sourced description) removes the duplicate JS shipped to the client and the duplicate re-render bug described in §2.\n\n**`src/components/pages/ProductPage.tsx:1`** is marked `\"use client\"` but uses no hooks — it's a pure composition of already-client child components (`PageHero`, `ProductBlocks`, `ContactCTA`). It can be a Server Component:\n\n```tsx\n// remove the \"use client\" directive — nothing in this file needs it\nimport Link from \"next/link\";\nimport type { Product } from \"@/lib/products\";\n...\nexport default function ProductPage({ product }: { product: Product }) { ... }\n```\n\nMinor, low-priority items (each component here only renders once or a handful of times, so these are hygiene, not hot-path fixes): `Trust.tsx`'s `ticks()` calls and `Manifesto.tsx`/`PageHero.tsx`/`Hero.tsx`'s `text.split(\" \")` calls recompute static derivations on every render of components that have no props/state driving re-renders — hoisting them to module scope costs nothing and removes the churn if those components ever do start re-rendering for unrelated reasons.\n",
